---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Nawtch | Free Calorie & Macro Tracker"
  description="Why Nawtch exists, how your data is stored, how diet and supplement content is sourced, and how the free tracker is funded."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  bodyClass="privacy"
  ads="rail"
>
  <header>
    <div class="header-left">
      <h1>About Nawtch</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">A free calorie, macro, and cost tracker, built and maintained by one person.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="ghost-btn" href="#" onclick="window.history.back(); return false;">← Back</a>
  </header>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Why Nawtch Exists</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        I built Nawtch because the trackers I tried kept putting basic features behind a paywall, or asked me to
        make an account just to log a meal.
        <br /><br />
        Nawtch is built and maintained by one person, and I use it every day myself.
        <br /><br />
        At one point I planned a paid tier. I scrapped it, because charging for features contradicted the reason
        the app exists.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">How Your Data Is Handled</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        There are no accounts. Your food, weight, and workout data never leaves your device. It is stored in your
        browser's IndexedDB, and there is no Nawtch server holding your logs.
        <br /><br />
        Because of that, clearing your browser's site data can erase everything. Export a full backup from <a href="/settings/">Settings</a> and keep it somewhere safe.
        Food searches and barcode scans are looked up through Open Food Facts, and ads and analytics are run by
        Google. The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what is collected.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">How the Content Is Sourced</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Each calculator names the formula or guideline it uses, so you can check the math.
        <br /><br />
        Diet and supplement pages present the evidence evenhandedly and never rank one option as the best. Where
        evidence is weak or missing, the page says so. For example, Whole30 has no independent clinical trials, and
        its page states that plainly.
        <br /><br />
        The peptides section sorts each substance into one of three tiers: FDA-approved, off-label or limited
        history, and unregulated research chemicals. Pages in the two unapproved tiers give no dosing or
        administration information. Peptide pages carry a "last verified" date, and the section is reviewed monthly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- If affiliate links are ever added, update this section, the Terms of Use, and the Privacy Policy. -->
  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">How Nawtch Is Funded</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Nawtch is free to use. It is supported by non-intrusive ads. There are no paywalls.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Not Medical Advice</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Nawtch is for education and personal tracking. It is not medical advice and does not diagnose or treat any
        condition. Talk to a qualified clinician before changing your diet, supplements, or medication. See the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Contact</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Questions, corrections, or a source you think I missed? Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="field-hint" style="margin-top:20px;">Written by Dallas, developer and nutrition nut.</p>
</BaseLayout>
